{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1087", "sample_idx": 19, "model_name": "mistralai/mistral-small-4-119b-2603", "content": "the social network is a brilliant, fast-paced drama that dives deep into the creation of facebook and the cutthroat world of silicon valley. directed by david fincher and written by aaron sorkin, the film is a masterclass in sharp dialogue, tense storytelling, and razor-sharp character dynamics.\n\nthe story follows mark zuckerberg (played by jesse eisenberg) as he drops out of harvard to build a social networking site called thefacebook with his best friend eduardo severin (andrew garfield). what starts as a college project quickly spirals into a billion-dollar empire, but the friendship between zuckerberg and severin fractures under the weight of ambition, betrayal, and legal battles. the film explores themes of ambition, loyalty, and the cost of success, all while painting a vivid portrait of the early days of social media.\n\njesse eisenberg’s performance as zuckerberg is electric—his portrayal of the socially awkward, driven genius is both unsettling and fascinating. andrew garfield shines as eduardo, the loyal friend turned victim of zuckerberg’s ruthless ambition. the supporting cast, including armie hammer as the winklevoss twins and max minghella as divya narendra, adds depth and humor to the story, while the legal drama between zuckerberg and his former partners (sean parker, played by justin timberlake) is gripping and full of tension.\n\nfincher’s direction is sleek and stylish, with a dark, moody aesthetic that perfectly captures the high-stakes world of tech and finance. the film’s pacing is relentless, with sorkin’s razor-sharp dialogue driving the story forward at a breakneck speed. the soundtrack, featuring tracks by trent reznor and atticus ross, adds an eerie, modern edge that fits the film’s themes of digital revolution and human connection.\n\nthe social network isn’t just a movie about facebook—it’s a commentary on the digital age, the people who shape it, and the personal costs of changing the world. it’s a must-watch for anyone interested in tech, business, or human drama, and it remains one of the best films of the 21st century.\n\nrating: 9.5/10", "logprobs": [{"token": "the", "logprob": -0.37151509523391724}, {"token": " social", "logprob": -0.0034185561817139387}, {"token": " network", "logprob": -1.1920928244535389e-07}, {"token": " is", "logprob": -0.6818562746047974}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.012009222991764545}, {"token": " brilliant", "logprob": -3.1764395236968994}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -1.4545565843582153}, {"token": " fast", "logprob": -0.6936167478561401}, {"token": "-p", "logprob": -3.2305197237292305e-05}, {"token": "aced", "logprob": -6.198863957251888e-06}, {"token": " drama", "logprob": -0.04718029126524925}, {"token": " that", "logprob": -0.03539488837122917}, {"token": " div", "logprob": -0.26389479637145996}, {"token": "es", "logprob": -1.1920928244535389e-07}, {"token": " deep", "logprob": -0.3144265115261078}, {"token": " into", "logprob": -1.5497195136049413e-06}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.0008120815036818385}, {"token": " creation", "logprob": -1.1539967060089111}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -0.01882426254451275}, {"token": " facebook", "logprob": -0.00036816971260122955}, {"token": " and", "logprob": -0.07451972365379333}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.003187577472999692}, {"token": " cut", "logprob": -4.387979030609131}, {"token": "th", "logprob": -5.829164365422912e-05}, {"token": "ro", "logprob": -6.437280717364047e-06}, {"token": "at", "logprob": -1.5497195136049413e-06}, {"token": " world", "logprob": -0.0007141662063077092}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -0.00346666993573308}, {"token": " silicon", "logprob": -0.4143349528312683}, {"token": " valley", "logprob": -7.629365427419543e-06}, {"token": ".", "logprob": -0.23903200030326843}, {"token": " directed", "logprob": -0.008766498416662216}, {"token": " by", "logprob": -0.002356254